    <string name="dsremo_outbound_otp_title">You\'re about to share an OTP</string>
    <string name="dsremo_outbound_otp_body">It looks like you\'re sending a one-time password to someone who just sent you an OTP message.\n\nThis is the most common scam pattern in India: fraudsters call or text claiming to be from a bank, CBI, FedEx, or a delivery service, and trick people into sharing the OTP they just received.\n\nNobody legitimate will ever ask you to share an OTP, PIN, or CVV.\n\nIf you\'re sure this is safe (e.g., you\'re manually relaying to another device of your own), tap Send Anyway after the 5-second hold.</string>
